                <dc:title>The Sinews of Peace</dc:title>
                <dc:title>Speech by Winston S. Churchill, Prime Minister of the United Kingdom, at Westminster College, Fulton, Missouri, USA</dc:title>
                <dc:creator>Churchill, Winston S.</dc:creator>
                <dc:date>1946-03-05</dc:date>

                <dc:coverage>Fulton</dc:coverage>
                <dc:coverage>Missouri</dc:coverage>
                <dc:coverage>United States</dc:coverage>

                <dc:publisher>North Atlantic Treaty Organization (NATO)</dc:publisher>
                <dc:contributor>North Atlantic Treaty Organization (NATO)</dc:contributor>
                <dc:description>The Sinews of Peace, often referred to as the Iron Curtain speech, was delivered by Winston Churchill on 5 March 1946, at Westminster College in Fulton, Missouri. In this speech, Churchill warned against the expansionist policies of the Soviet Union and advocated for a strong alliance between Western nations to counter the threat of communism.</dc:description>

